	(text "V_{F}(Typ)= 1.75 V\nR = 77.5 Ω\nV = (3.3 - 1.75)\nI = 20 mA\n77.5 Ω is an uncommon resistor, maybe change to something else\n\n\nV_{F}(Typ)= 1.75 V\nR = 330 Ω\nV = (3.3 - 1.75)\nI = 4.7 mA\nFor a status LED, 330 Ω (about 4.7 mA) should be sufficient. \nIt's bright enough for most indicator LEDs and stays well \nwithin the pin's limits"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 113.03 0)
